"\n<div class=\"brand-bar\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"brand-logo\"><div class=\"brand-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div></div>\n<header class=\"lk-hd\"><div class=\"lk-topic\"><svg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 21s6-5.3 6-10a6 6 0 1 0-12 0c0 4.7 6 10 6 10z\"></path><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"11\" r=\"2.2\"></circle></svg></div><div class=\"lk-kicker\">Lektion</div><div class=\"lk-big\">34</div><h1>형용사·명사와 전치사</h1><div class=\"lk-de\">Adjektive und Nomen mit Präpositionen</div><div class=\"lk-intro\">18과에서 동사마다 함께 쓰는 전치사가 정해져 있다는 것을 배웠어요 — warten auf · denken an.<br>형용사와 명사도 마찬가지예요 — <strong>stolz auf</strong> 자랑스러운 · <strong>Angst vor</strong> 두려움.<br>이 과에서는 자주 쓰는 형용사 + 전치사와 명사 + 전치사를 전치사별로 정리하고, 동사·형용사·명사의 짝, da(r)-·wo(r)-로 받는 법, 문장을 잇는 법을 연습해요.<div class=\"x-goals\"><div class=\"x-goals-t\">이 과에서 익힐 것</div><div class=\"x-goal\">자주 쓰는 형용사 + 전치사를 전치사와 격까지 함께 외워요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">형용사 + 전치사를 sein·werden 문장에 넣어요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">자주 쓰는 명사 + 전치사를 외워요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">동사·형용사·명사의 짝에서 같은 전치사와 다른 전치사를 구별해요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">사람은 auf ihn·auf wen, 사물은 darauf·worauf로 받고 물어요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">문장이 이어지면 da(r)- + dass·zu로 연결해요</div></div></div></header>\n<div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge review-badge\">복습</span><span class=\"sub-title\">17·18·28과 복습</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Ich warte ____ den Bus.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) nach</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) für</button></div><div class=\"qe\">warten auf + 4격 (18과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Ich freue mich ____ das Wochenende. <span class=\"qh\">주말이 기다려져요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) auf</button></div><div class=\"qe\">앞으로의 일 → auf (17과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> ____ wartest du? — Auf meinen Freund.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Auf was</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Auf wen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Worauf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Wen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">사람 → 전치사 + wen (18과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Ich habe keine Lust, heute ____. <span class=\"qh\">요리하는 것</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) zu kochen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) kochen zu</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) gekocht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) kochen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Lust haben 뒤에는 zu 부정형이 와요(28과). zu는 원형 바로 앞, 문장 맨 끝에 놓여요.</div></div></div>\n<section id=\"sec-A\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">A</span><h2>한국어로 먼저 보기</h2></div><p>한국어는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">형용사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">형용사</span>사람이나 사물이 어떤지를 나타내는 말이에요. 명사 앞에서는 어미가 붙어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Buch ist gut. · das gute Buch</span></span></span>·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명사</span>사람·동물·물건·장소·생각의 이름이 되는 말이에요. 독일어 명사는 첫 글자를 대문자로 써요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Tisch 책상 · die Liebe 사랑</span></span></span> 앞의 말에 조사를 붙여요 — '아들이 자랑스럽다', '결과에 만족하다', '음악에 관심이 있다'.<br>조사는 '이·에·에게'처럼 여러 가지예요.<br>독일어는 형용사와 명사마다 함께 쓰는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>와 격이 정해져 있어요. 한국어 조사로는 짐작할 수 없어서 함께 외워야 해요.</p><div class=\"dgm\"><div class=\"dgm-cap\">한국어 조사와 상관없는 독일어 전치사</div><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>한국어</th><th>독일어</th><th>전치사 + 격</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>아들<strong>이</strong> 자랑스럽다</td><td><strong>stolz auf</strong> den Sohn</td><td>auf + 4격</td></tr><tr><td>결과<strong>에</strong> 만족하다</td><td><strong>zufrieden mit</strong> dem Ergebnis</td><td>mit + 3격</td></tr><tr><td>독일 문화<strong>에</strong> 관심이 있다</td><td><strong>interessiert an</strong> der deutschen Kultur</td><td>an + 3격</td></tr><tr><td>그 사람<strong>과</strong> 결혼했다</td><td><strong>verheiratet mit</strong> ihm</td><td>mit + 3격</td></tr><tr><td>개<strong>를</strong> 무서워함</td><td><strong>Angst vor</strong> dem Hund</td><td>vor + 3격</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"dgm-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span> + 전치사(18과)처럼 '형용사 + 전치사 + 격'을 한 줄로 외우고, 예문을 하나씩 붙여 둬요.</div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-B\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">B</span><h2>형용사 + 전치사 — 전치사별로 외우기</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">형용사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">형용사</span>사람이나 사물이 어떤지를 나타내는 말이에요. 명사 앞에서는 어미가 붙어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Buch ist gut. · das gute Buch</span></span></span>도 함께 쓰는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>가 정해져 있어요 — stolz <strong>auf</strong> 자랑스러운 · zufrieden <strong>mit</strong> 만족한.</p></div></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" alt=\"Die Eltern sind stolz auf ihren Sohn. 부모님은 아들이 자랑스러워요.\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><div><span class=\"ph-de\">Die Eltern sind <strong>stolz auf</strong> ihren Sohn.</span><span class=\"ph-ko\">부모님은 아들이 자랑스러워요.</span></div></figcaption></figure><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>전치사</th><th>형용사</th><th>예</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>auf + 4격</td><td><strong>stolz</strong> 자랑스러운 · <strong>neugierig</strong> 궁금한 · <strong>gespannt</strong> 기대되는 · <strong>böse</strong> · <strong>wütend</strong> 화난 · <strong>neidisch</strong> 부러워하는 · <strong>eifersüchtig</strong> 질투하는 · <strong>angewiesen</strong> 의존하는</td><td>Ich bin <strong>stolz auf</strong> meinen Sohn.</td></tr><tr><td>an + 3격</td><td><strong>interessiert</strong> 관심 있는 · <strong>beteiligt</strong> 참여한 · <strong>schuld</strong> 책임이 있는 · <strong>reich</strong> 풍부한</td><td>Sie ist <strong>interessiert an</strong> Kunst.</td></tr><tr><td>an + 4격</td><td><strong>gewöhnt</strong> 익숙한</td><td>Ich bin <strong>an</strong> das Wetter <strong>gewöhnt</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>für + 4격</td><td><strong>verantwortlich</strong> 책임 있는 · <strong>zuständig</strong> 담당하는 · <strong>bekannt</strong> ~⁠로 유명한 · <strong>dankbar</strong> 고마운 · <strong>geeignet</strong> 적합한 · <strong>typisch</strong> 전형적인</td><td>Er ist <strong>verantwortlich für</strong> das Projekt.</td></tr><tr><td>mit + 3격</td><td><strong>zufrieden</strong> 만족한 · <strong>einverstanden</strong> 동의하는 · <strong>verheiratet</strong> 결혼한 · <strong>befreundet</strong> 친한 · <strong>fertig</strong> 끝낸 · <strong>vertraut</strong> 잘 아는</td><td>Bist du <strong>fertig mit</strong> der Arbeit?</td></tr><tr><td>von + 3격</td><td><strong>abhängig</strong> 의존하는 · <strong>begeistert</strong> 열광한 · <strong>überzeugt</strong> 확신하는 · <strong>enttäuscht</strong> 실망한 · <strong>beeindruckt</strong> 감명받은</td><td>Ich bin <strong>überzeugt von</strong> der Idee.</td></tr><tr><td>über + 4격</td><td><strong>froh</strong> 기쁜 · <strong>glücklich</strong> 행복한 · <strong>traurig</strong> 슬픈 · <strong>überrascht</strong> 놀란 · <strong>verärgert</strong> 화가 난 · <strong>informiert</strong> 알고 있는</td><td>Wir sind <strong>froh über</strong> die Nachricht.</td></tr><tr><td>zu + 3격</td><td><strong>bereit</strong> 준비된 · <strong>fähig</strong> 할 수 있는 · <strong>freundlich</strong> · <strong>nett</strong> 친절한</td><td>Sie ist immer <strong>nett zu</strong> mir.</td></tr><tr><td>in + 4격</td><td><strong>verliebt</strong> 사랑에 빠진</td><td>Er ist <strong>verliebt in</strong> seine Kollegin.</td></tr><tr><td>nach + 3격</td><td><strong>verrückt</strong> 몹시 좋아하는 · <strong>süchtig</strong> 중독된</td><td>Sie ist <strong>verrückt nach</strong> Schokolade.</td></tr><tr><td>bei + 3격</td><td><strong>beliebt</strong> 인기 있는</td><td>Der Lehrer ist <strong>beliebt bei</strong> den Schülern.</td></tr><tr><td>vor + 3격</td><td><strong>sicher</strong> 안전한</td><td>Hier bist du <strong>sicher vor</strong> dem Regen.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-key\"><span class=\"co-badge \">추상적인 auf · über는 거의 4격</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">auf·über가 장소가 아닌 뜻으로 쓰이면 거의 언제나 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">4격<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">4격</span>주로 '~을/를'을 나타내는 자리예요. 동작을 받는 대상이고, für·ohne 같은 전치사 뒤에도 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich sehe den Mann. 그 남자를 봐요.</span></span></span>이에요 — stolz auf <strong>den</strong> Sohn · froh über <strong>die</strong> Nachricht.<br>an·vor·in은 낱말마다 다르니 격까지 함께 외워요 — interessiert an <strong>der</strong> Kunst(<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">3격<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">3격</span>주로 '~에게'를 나타내는 자리예요. helfen·danken 같은 동사와 mit·bei·zu 같은 전치사 뒤에도 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich gebe dem Kind ein Buch. 아이에게 책을 줘요.</span></span></span>) · gewöhnt an <strong>das</strong> Wetter(4격).</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">형용사 + 전치사</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Ich bin sehr stolz ____ dich.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) über</button></div><div class=\"qe\">stolz auf + 4격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Bist du zufrieden ____ deinem neuen Job?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) mit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) von</button></div><div class=\"qe\">zufrieden mit + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Er ist interessiert ____ Politik.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) an</button></div><div class=\"qe\">interessiert an + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Ich bin gespannt ____ das Ergebnis. <span class=\"qh\">결과가 기대돼요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) nach</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) über</button></div><div class=\"qe\">gespannt auf + 4격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Wer ist verantwortlich ____ den Fehler?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) von</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) an</button></div><div class=\"qe\">verantwortlich für + 4격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Wir sind enttäuscht ____ dem Film.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) von</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) mit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) über</button></div><div class=\"qe\">enttäuscht von + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">7.</strong> Sie ist seit fünf Jahren verheiratet ____ einem Deutschen.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) bei</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) zu</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) mit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) an</button></div><div class=\"qe\">verheiratet mit + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">8.</strong> Bist du bereit ____ einem Neuanfang?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) zu</button></div><div class=\"qe\">bereit zu + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">9.</strong> Ich bin noch nicht ____ das kalte Wetter gewöhnt.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) zu</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) mit</button></div><div class=\"qe\">gewöhnt an + 4격.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-C\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">C</span><h2>문장 속 자리</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">형용사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">형용사</span>사람이나 사물이 어떤지를 나타내는 말이에요. 명사 앞에서는 어미가 붙어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Buch ist gut. · das gute Buch</span></span></span> + <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>는 주로 sein 뒤에 오고, 전치사 부분은 형용사 앞에 두는 게 보통이에요 — Ich bin <strong>mit dem Ergebnis</strong> zufrieden.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-scroll\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 244\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"형용사와 전치사구의 자리 — 기본은 전치사구가 형용사 앞, nicht는 형용사 바로 앞이에요\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><marker id=\"adj_pp_order-ink\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mki\"/></marker><marker id=\"adj_pp_order-acc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mka\"/></marker><marker id=\"adj_pp_order-ok\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mko\"/></marker><marker id=\"adj_pp_order-no\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mkn\"/></marker><marker id=\"adj_pp_order-w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mkw\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"14.0\" y=\"46.0\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">기본</text><rect x=\"96.0\" y=\"20.0\" width=\"46.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"119.3\" y=\"46.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">Ich</text><rect x=\"149.7\" y=\"20.0\" width=\"46.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"173.0\" y=\"46.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">bin</text><rect x=\"203.3\" y=\"20.0\" width=\"169.9\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxo\"/><text x=\"288.3\" y=\"46.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-okt\" font-weight=\"700\">mit dem Ergebnis</text><rect x=\"380.3\" y=\"20.0\" width=\"105.8\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxa\"/><text x=\"433.2\" y=\"46.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\" font-weight=\"700\">zufrieden.</text><text x=\"14.0\" y=\"112.0\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">말할 때</text><rect x=\"96.0\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"46.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"119.3\" y=\"112.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">Ich</text><rect x=\"149.7\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"46.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"173.0\" y=\"112.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">bin</text><rect x=\"203.3\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"100.0\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxa\"/><text x=\"253.3\" y=\"112.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\" font-weight=\"700\">zufrieden</text><rect x=\"310.3\" y=\"86.0\" width=\"175.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxo\"/><text x=\"398.2\" y=\"112.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-okt\" font-weight=\"700\">mit dem Ergebnis.</text><text x=\"14.0\" y=\"178.0\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">부정</text><rect x=\"96.0\" y=\"152.0\" width=\"46.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"119.3\" y=\"178.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">Ich</text><rect x=\"149.7\" y=\"152.0\" width=\"46.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"173.0\" y=\"178.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">bin</text><rect x=\"203.3\" y=\"152.0\" width=\"169.9\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxo\"/><text x=\"288.3\" y=\"178.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-okt\" font-weight=\"700\">mit dem Ergebnis</text><rect x=\"380.3\" y=\"152.0\" width=\"63.2\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxn\"/><text x=\"411.9\" y=\"178.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-not\" font-weight=\"700\">nicht</text><rect x=\"450.5\" y=\"152.0\" width=\"105.8\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxa\"/><text x=\"503.4\" y=\"178.1\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\" font-weight=\"700\">zufrieden.</text><text x=\"300.0\" y=\"232.0\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-m\">초록 = 전치사구 · 파랑 = 형용사 · 빨강 = nicht</text></svg></div><figcaption>전치사구는 보통 형용사 앞 — 말할 때는 뒤에도 와요</figcaption></figure><p>말할 때는 전치사구를 형용사 뒤에 두기도 해요.</p><div class=\"exl\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich bin <strong>mit dem Ergebnis</strong> zufrieden.</span><span class=\"exl-nt\">기본 — 전치사구가 앞</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">나는 결과에 만족해요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich bin zufrieden <strong>mit dem Ergebnis</strong>.</span><span class=\"exl-nt\">말할 때 — 전치사구가 뒤</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">나는 결과에 만족해요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich bin <strong>mit dem Ergebnis</strong> nicht zufrieden.</span><span class=\"exl-nt\">nicht는 형용사 바로 앞(9과)</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">결과에 만족하지 않아요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Er wird <strong>auf seine Tochter</strong> stolz sein.</span><span class=\"exl-nt\">미래형</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">그는 딸을 자랑스러워할 거예요.</span></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">명사 앞에 쓰면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">형용사 + 전치사를 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명사</span>사람·동물·물건·장소·생각의 이름이 되는 말이에요. 독일어 명사는 첫 글자를 대문자로 써요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Tisch 책상 · die Liebe 사랑</span></span></span> 앞에 쓰면 전치사구가 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">관사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">관사</span>명사 앞에 붙어 그 명사의 성·수·격과, 정해진 대상인지 아닌지를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Hund 그 개 · ein Hund 개 한 마리</span></span></span>와 형용사 사이에 들어가요(32과의 늘어난 분사구와 같은 모양).<br>der <strong>auf seine Tochter</strong> stolz<span class=\"x-e\">e</span> Vater 딸을 자랑스러워하는 아버지 — 글에서 가끔 보여요.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-D\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">D</span><h2>명사 + 전치사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명사</span>사람·동물·물건·장소·생각의 이름이 되는 말이에요. 독일어 명사는 첫 글자를 대문자로 써요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Tisch 책상 · die Liebe 사랑</span></span></span>도 마찬가지예요 — Angst <strong>vor</strong> 두려움 · Lust <strong>auf</strong> 하고 싶은 마음.</p></div></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" alt=\"Das Kind hat Angst vor dem Hund. 아이가 개를 무서워해요. vor 뒤는 3격이에요.\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><div><span class=\"ph-de\">Das Kind hat <strong>Angst vor dem</strong> Hund.</span><span class=\"ph-ko\">아이가 개를 무서워해요. vor 뒤는 3격이에요.</span></div></figcaption></figure><p>명사도 함께 쓰는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>가 정해져 있어요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">형용사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">형용사</span>사람이나 사물이 어떤지를 나타내는 말이에요. 명사 앞에서는 어미가 붙어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Buch ist gut. · das gute Buch</span></span></span>에서 온 명사는 원래 말의 전치사를 따르는 경우가 많아요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>전치사</th><th>명사</th><th>예</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>auf + 4격</td><td><strong>Lust</strong> 하고 싶은 마음 · <strong>Hoffnung</strong> 희망 · <strong>Antwort</strong> 대답 · <strong>Einfluss</strong> 영향 · <strong>Anspruch</strong> 권리 · <strong>Rücksicht</strong> 배려</td><td>Ich habe <strong>Lust auf</strong> einen Kaffee.</td></tr><tr><td>an + 3격</td><td><strong>Interesse</strong> 관심 · <strong>Kritik</strong> 비판 · <strong>Mangel</strong> 부족 · <strong>Teilnahme</strong> 참가 · <strong>Zweifel</strong> 의심 · <strong>Freude</strong> 즐거움</td><td>Es gibt einen <strong>Mangel an</strong> Fachkräften.</td></tr><tr><td>für + 4격</td><td><strong>Grund</strong> 이유 · <strong>Verständnis</strong> 이해 · <strong>Beispiel</strong> 예 · <strong>Dank</strong> 감사 · <strong>Lösung</strong> 해결책</td><td>Das ist ein gutes <strong>Beispiel für</strong> das Problem.</td></tr><tr><td>über + 4격</td><td><strong>Informationen</strong> 정보 · <strong>Diskussion</strong> 토론 · <strong>Freude</strong> 기쁨 · <strong>Ärger</strong> 분노</td><td>Haben Sie <strong>Informationen über</strong> den Kurs?</td></tr><tr><td>vor + 3격</td><td><strong>Angst</strong> 두려움 · <strong>Respekt</strong> 존중 · <strong>Warnung</strong> 경고</td><td>Viele Kinder haben <strong>Angst vor</strong> dem Zahnarzt.</td></tr><tr><td>mit + 3격</td><td><strong>Erfahrung</strong> 경험 · <strong>Kontakt</strong> 연락 · <strong>Problem</strong> 문제</td><td>Ich habe <strong>Erfahrung mit</strong> Kindern.</td></tr><tr><td>nach + 3격</td><td><strong>Frage</strong> 질문 · <strong>Suche</strong> 찾기 · <strong>Sehnsucht</strong> 그리움 · <strong>Nachfrage</strong> 수요</td><td>Die <strong>Suche nach</strong> einer Wohnung ist schwer.</td></tr><tr><td>zu + 3격</td><td><strong>Beziehung</strong> 관계 · <strong>Einladung</strong> 초대 · <strong>Einstellung</strong> 태도 · <strong>Zugang</strong> 접근</td><td>Ich habe eine gute <strong>Beziehung zu</strong> meinen Eltern.</td></tr><tr><td>um + 4격</td><td><strong>Bitte</strong> 부탁 · <strong>Sorge</strong> 걱정</td><td>Ich habe eine <strong>Bitte um</strong> Hilfe.</td></tr><tr><td>von + 3격</td><td><strong>Abhängigkeit</strong> 의존</td><td>die <strong>Abhängigkeit vom</strong> Handy</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">명사 + 전치사</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Ich habe keine Lust ____ Fußball.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) zu</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Lust auf + 4격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Hast du Angst ____ Spinnen?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) von</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) vor</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Angst vor + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Was ist der Grund ____ deine Entscheidung?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) zu</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) von</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Grund für + 4격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Er hat großes Interesse ____ Geschichte.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) von</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Interesse an + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Ich habe eine Frage ____ dem Preis.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) nach</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) an</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Frage nach + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Danke für die Einladung ____ deiner Party!</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) zu</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) auf</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Einladung zu + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">7.</strong> Wir haben viel Erfahrung ____ diesem Programm.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) mit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) von</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) in</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Erfahrung mit + 3격.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-E\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">E</span><h2>같은 전치사의 짝 — 동사 · 형용사 · 명사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">같은 뜻의 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">형용사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">형용사</span>사람이나 사물이 어떤지를 나타내는 말이에요. 명사 앞에서는 어미가 붙어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Buch ist gut. · das gute Buch</span></span></span>·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명사</span>사람·동물·물건·장소·생각의 이름이 되는 말이에요. 독일어 명사는 첫 글자를 대문자로 써요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Tisch 책상 · die Liebe 사랑</span></span></span>는 대부분 같은 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>를 써요 — sich freuen über · froh über · die Freude über.</p></div></div><p>하나를 외우면 나머지도 쉽게 외울 수 있어요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>동사</th><th>형용사</th><th>명사</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>sich freuen <strong>über</strong></td><td>froh <strong>über</strong></td><td>die Freude <strong>über</strong></td></tr><tr><td>sich ärgern <strong>über</strong></td><td>verärgert <strong>über</strong></td><td>der Ärger <strong>über</strong></td></tr><tr><td>teilnehmen <strong>an</strong></td><td>beteiligt <strong>an</strong></td><td>die Teilnahme <strong>an</strong></td></tr><tr><td>abhängen <strong>von</strong></td><td>abhängig <strong>von</strong></td><td>die Abhängigkeit <strong>von</strong></td></tr><tr><td>hoffen <strong>auf</strong></td><td>—</td><td>die Hoffnung <strong>auf</strong></td></tr><tr><td>antworten <strong>auf</strong></td><td>—</td><td>die Antwort <strong>auf</strong></td></tr><tr><td>bitten <strong>um</strong></td><td>—</td><td>die Bitte <strong>um</strong></td></tr><tr><td>fragen <strong>nach</strong></td><td>—</td><td>die Frage <strong>nach</strong></td></tr><tr><td>sich erinnern <strong>an</strong></td><td>—</td><td>die Erinnerung <strong>an</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-warn\"><span class=\"co-badge co-warn\">전치사가 달라지는 짝</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">sich interessieren <strong>für</strong> / interessiert <strong>an</strong> / das Interesse <strong>an</strong>(für도 가능)<br>sich begeistern <strong>für</strong> / begeistert <strong>von</strong> / die Begeisterung <strong>für</strong><br>이런 짝은 따로 표시해서 외워요.</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">짝 맞추기</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> sich interessieren für → interessiert ____</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) an</button></div><div class=\"qe\">형용사는 interessiert an.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> sich begeistern für → begeistert ____</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) von</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) an</button></div><div class=\"qe\">형용사는 begeistert von.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> bitten um → die Bitte ____</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) nach</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) um</button></div><div class=\"qe\">명사도 um.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> sich ärgern über → der Ärger ____</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) an</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) über</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) auf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) mit</button></div><div class=\"qe\">명사도 über.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-F\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">F</span><h2>대명사로 받기와 문장 잇기</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">사람은 auf ihn, 물건이나 일은 darauf로 받아요. 문장이 이어지면 darauf, dass …로 말해요.</p></div></div><p>18과의 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span> + <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>와 같은 규칙이에요. 사람은 전치사 + <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">인칭대명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">인칭대명사</span>사람이나 사물을 가리키는 ich·du·er·sie·es 같은 대명사예요. 격에 따라 모양이 바뀌어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich → mir → mich</span></span></span>, 사물·일은 da(r)- + 전치사로 받아요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>사람</th><th>사물 · 일</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>대명사</td><td>Ich bin stolz <strong>auf ihn</strong>.</td><td>Ich bin stolz <strong>darauf</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>질문</td><td><strong>Auf wen</strong> bist du stolz?</td><td><strong>Worauf</strong> bist du stolz?</td></tr><tr><td>대명사</td><td>Ich habe Angst <strong>vor ihm</strong>.</td><td>Ich habe Angst <strong>davor</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>질문</td><td><strong>Vor wem</strong> hast du Angst?</td><td><strong>Wovor</strong> hast du Angst?</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>문장이 이어질 때 — da(r)- + dass · zu</h3><p>전치사 뒤에 문장이 통째로 오면 da(r)- + 전치사를 먼저 놓고 dass 문장이나 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">zu 부정형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">zu 부정형</span>zu + 동사원형으로 된 형태예요. 문장 끝에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich versuche, früh aufzustehen.</span></span></span>을 이어요.</p><div class=\"exl\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich bin stolz <strong>darauf</strong>, <strong>dass</strong> ich die Prüfung bestanden habe.</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">시험에 합격한 게 자랑스러워요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich habe Angst <strong>davor</strong>, allein <strong>zu</strong> sein.</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">혼자 있는 게 두려워요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Er ist <strong>daran</strong> interessiert, im Ausland <strong>zu</strong> arbeiten.</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">그는 외국에서 일하는 데 관심이 있어요.</span></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">da(r)-를 빼기도 해요</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">Lust haben · bereit sein · Angst haben 뒤의 zu 부정형에서는 da(r)-를 자주 빼요.<br>Hast du Lust, ins Kino <strong>zu</strong> gehen? · Ich bin bereit, dir <strong>zu</strong> helfen.<br><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명사</span>사람·동물·물건·장소·생각의 이름이 되는 말이에요. 독일어 명사는 첫 글자를 대문자로 써요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Tisch 책상 · die Liebe 사랑</span></span></span>만 올 때는 전치사를 꼭 써요 — Hast du <strong>Lust auf</strong> Kino?</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">대명사와 문장 잇기</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Bist du zufrieden mit dem Hotel? — Ja, ich bin sehr zufrieden ____.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) damit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) womit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) mit es</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) mit ihm</button></div><div class=\"qe\">사물 → da + mit.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> ____ bist du so stolz? — Auf mein neues Fahrrad.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Auf wen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Auf was für</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Wofür</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Worauf</button></div><div class=\"qe\">사물 질문 → wor + auf.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> ____ hast du Angst? — Vor meinem Chef.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Wovor</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Vor wen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Wovon</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Vor wem</button></div><div class=\"qe\">사람 → vor + 3격 wem.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Ich freue mich ____, dass du gestern gekommen bist.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) darauf</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) über es</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) darüber</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) dafür</button></div><div class=\"qe\">이미 일어난 기쁜 일 → darüber + dass (앞으로의 일이면 darauf).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Ich habe keine Lust, ____. <span class=\"qh\">오늘 청소하는 것</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) darauf heute aufräumen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) heute aufzuräumen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) heute aufräumen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) auf heute aufzuräumen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Lust haben + zu 부정형.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-G\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">G</span><h2>가장 많이 하는 실수</h2></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 1</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">한국어 조사대로 전치사를 골라요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin stolz über meinen Sohn.<span class=\"tx-n\">'~⁠이 자랑스럽다'를 짐작으로</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin stolz auf meinen Sohn.<span class=\"tx-n\">아들이 자랑스러워요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">형용사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">형용사</span>사람이나 사물이 어떤지를 나타내는 말이에요. 명사 앞에서는 어미가 붙어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Buch ist gut. · das gute Buch</span></span></span>마다 정해진 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>가 있어요 — stolz auf + <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">4격<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">4격</span>주로 '~을/를'을 나타내는 자리예요. 동작을 받는 대상이고, für·ohne 같은 전치사 뒤에도 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich sehe den Mann. 그 남자를 봐요.</span></span></span>.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 2</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">전치사 뒤의 격을 틀려요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin zufrieden mit das Ergebnis.<span class=\"tx-n\">1·4격 그대로</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin zufrieden mit dem Ergebnis.<span class=\"tx-n\">결과에 만족해요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">mit은 늘 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">3격<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">3격</span>주로 '~에게'를 나타내는 자리예요. helfen·danken 같은 동사와 mit·bei·zu 같은 전치사 뒤에도 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich gebe dem Kind ein Buch. 아이에게 책을 줘요.</span></span></span>이에요(14과).</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 3</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">동사의 전치사를 형용사에 그대로 써요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin interessiert für Musik.<span class=\"tx-n\">sich interessieren für에서 옮김</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin interessiert an Musik.<span class=\"tx-n\">음악에 관심이 있어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">interessiert·begeistert처럼 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>와 전치사가 다른 짝은 따로 외워요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 4</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">사물을 전치사 + es로 받아요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin stolz auf es.<span class=\"tx-n\">사물에 auf es</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich bin stolz darauf.<span class=\"tx-n\">그게 자랑스러워요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">사물·일은 da(r)- + 전치사예요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 5</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">Lust auf 뒤에 zu 부정형을 붙여요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe Lust auf ins Kino zu gehen.<span class=\"tx-n\">전치사 + 문장</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich habe Lust, ins Kino zu gehen. · Ich habe Lust aufs Kino.<span class=\"tx-n\">영화 보러 가고 싶어요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명사</span>사람·동물·물건·장소·생각의 이름이 되는 말이에요. 독일어 명사는 첫 글자를 대문자로 써요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Tisch 책상 · die Liebe 사랑</span></span></span>가 오면 auf, 문장(<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">zu 부정형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">zu 부정형</span>zu + 동사원형으로 된 형태예요. 문장 끝에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich versuche, früh aufzustehen.</span></span></span>)이 오면 쉼표 뒤에 이어요.</div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">실수 피하기</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Wir sind froh von die gute Nachricht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Wir sind froh über der guten Nachricht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Wir sind froh über die gute Nachricht.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Wir sind froh auf die gute Nachricht.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">froh über + 4격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Hast du Angst darvor?</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Hast du Angst davor?</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Hast du Angst wovor?</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Hast du Angst vor es?</button></div><div class=\"qe\">사물 → da + vor.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Sie ist sehr begeistert von dem Konzert.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Sie ist sehr begeistert über dem Konzert.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Sie ist sehr begeistert an dem Konzert.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Sie ist sehr begeistert für das Konzert.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">begeistert von + 3격.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ich bin verantwortlich für der Planung.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Ich bin verantwortlich für die Planung.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Ich bin verantwortlich über die Planung.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ich bin verantwortlich an der Planung.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">verantwortlich für + 4격.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-H\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">H</span><h2>참고</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">사전에서 찾기</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">사전의 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">형용사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">형용사</span>사람이나 사물이 어떤지를 나타내는 말이에요. 명사 앞에서는 어미가 붙어요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Buch ist gut. · das gute Buch</span></span></span>·<span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명사</span>사람·동물·물건·장소·생각의 이름이 되는 말이에요. 독일어 명사는 첫 글자를 대문자로 써요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: der Tisch 책상 · die Liebe 사랑</span></span></span> 항목에는 함께 쓰는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">전치사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">전치사</span>명사·대명사 앞에 붙어 장소·시간·이유 같은 관계를 나타내는 말이에요. 뒤에 올 격을 정해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: mit dem Bus · für dich</span></span></span>와 격이 나와 있어요 — stolz (auf + Akk.) · Angst (vor + Dat.).<br>Akk.는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">4격<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">4격</span>주로 '~을/를'을 나타내는 자리예요. 동작을 받는 대상이고, für·ohne 같은 전치사 뒤에도 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich sehe den Mann. 그 남자를 봐요.</span></span></span>, Dat.는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">3격<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">3격</span>주로 '~에게'를 나타내는 자리예요. helfen·danken 같은 동사와 mit·bei·zu 같은 전치사 뒤에도 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich gebe dem Kind ein Buch. 아이에게 책을 줘요.</span></span></span>이에요.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">외우는 방법</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">전치사별로 묶어 외우되, 문장 하나를 함께 외워요 — auf + 4격: stolz auf · gespannt auf · Lust auf → Ich bin gespannt auf den Film.<br>시험의 빈칸 채우기 문항에서 자주 나오는 결합이에요.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">18과와 함께 보기</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span> + 전치사(18과), <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">재귀동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">재귀동사</span>재귀대명사와 함께 쓰는 동사예요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: sich freuen · sich waschen</span></span></span> + 전치사(17과), 이 과의 형용사·명사 + 전치사를 한 표로 모아 두면 복습하기 좋아요.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-I\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">I</span><h2>바로 쓰는 문장 · 일상 회화</h2></div><p>감정과 생각을 말할 때 자주 쓰는 문장이에요.</p><div class=\"exl talk-l\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich bin sehr <strong>stolz auf</strong> dich.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 빈 제어 슈톨츠 아우프 디히</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">네가 정말 자랑스러워.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Bist du <strong>zufrieden mit</strong> dem Ergebnis?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">비스트 두 추프리덴 미트 뎀 에어게브니스</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">결과에 만족해?</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich habe keine <strong>Lust auf</strong> Pizza.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 하베 카이네 루스트 아우프 피차</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">피자는 별로 안 당겨.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich bin <strong>gespannt darauf</strong>.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 빈 게슈판트 다라우프</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">그게 정말 기대돼.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Hast du <strong>Angst vor</strong> Hunden?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">하스트 두 앙스트 포어 훈덴</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">개 무서워해?</span></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"summary\"><div class=\"summary-card\"><h2 class=\"sum-title\">이 과 정리</h2><div><div class=\"sum-li\">형용사·명사도 함께 쓰는 전치사와 격이 정해져 있어요 — 한국어 조사로 짐작하지 않아요</div><div class=\"sum-li\">auf + 4격: stolz · gespannt · neugierig · Lust · Hoffnung / mit + 3격: zufrieden · verheiratet · fertig · Erfahrung</div><div class=\"sum-li\">an + 3격: interessiert · Interesse · Kritik · Mangel / für + 4격: verantwortlich · bekannt · Grund · Beispiel</div><div class=\"sum-li\">von + 3격: abhängig · begeistert · überzeugt · enttäuscht / über + 4격: froh · traurig · Informationen</div><div class=\"sum-li\">vor + 3격: Angst · Respekt / nach + 3격: Frage · Suche / zu + 3격: bereit · nett · Beziehung · Einladung</div><div class=\"sum-li\">동사·형용사·명사는 대부분 같은 전치사, 다른 짝은 따로 — interessieren für / interessiert an</div><div class=\"sum-li\">사람은 auf ihn · auf wen, 사물은 darauf · worauf, 문장은 da(r)- + dass · zu</div></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\" style=\"margin-top:20px\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">다음 ⏭ 35과</span><div>35과에서는 접두어와 접미사로 단어를 만드는 법을 배워요 — ankommen → die Ankunft · lesen → lesbar · Glück → glücklich.</div></div></section><section id=\"solutions\" class=\"solutions\"><h2 class=\"sol-title\">Lösungen — 정답 모아보기</h2><div class=\"sol-grid\"><div><b>17·18·28과 복습</b>1. auf · 2. auf · 3. Auf wen · 4. zu kochen</div><div><b>형용사 + 전치사</b>1. auf · 2. mit · 3. an · 4. auf · 5. für · 6. von · 7. mit · 8. zu · 9. an</div><div><b>명사 + 전치사</b>1. auf · 2. vor · 3. für · 4. an · 5. nach · 6. zu · 7. mit</div><div><b>짝 맞추기</b>1. an · 2. von · 3. um · 4. über</div><div><b>대명사와 문장 잇기</b>1. damit · 2. Worauf · 3. Vor wem · 4. darüber · 5. heute aufzuräumen</div><div><b>실수 피하기</b>1. Wir sind froh über die gute Nachricht. · 2. Hast du Angst davor? · 3. Sie ist sehr begeistert von dem Konzert. · 4. Ich bin verantwortlich für die Planung.</div></div></section>\n<div class=\"brand-foot\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"foot-logo\"><div class=\"foot-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div><div class=\"foot-tag\">Innovative Learning Beyond the Traditional</div></div>\n"